    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly! it's like the \"pro\" side is looking toward a better future for these kids, while the \"anti\" side is just using systemic arguments to keep things exactly how they are. if you had to pick which side has the more logical foundation for actual student success, which one would it be? isn't it more logical to empower the individual student than to protect a failing institution?",
